From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anas <assosbs9@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:23:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/44] totk: the game's main thread asks for user-interactive
 QoS, so macOS keeps the frame's submission on the performance cores
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It kept the launcher's unspecified QoS (the log's "本线程 QoS 0"): on a fanless MacBook Air M5 the submit thread's clock fell
from 3.5 to 1.3-1.8 GHz a few minutes into play, its CPU time per frame rose from 5 to 15 ms and Tears of the Kingdom ran
outdoors at 40-50 fps with the GPU at 13 ms. The threads CreateThread makes were already user-interactive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TFGN95PNfagSjomeEnf2po
---
 shared/runtime/threads.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shared/runtime/threads.c b/shared/runtime/threads.c
index 42cbfb9dd1119040613f0c12b8b4af7f66c1a11b..be1fa505e752ee992af50d6c35bc67348712a40b 100644
--- a/shared/runtime/threads.c
+++ b/shared/runtime/threads.c
@@ -834,6 +834,11 @@ uint32_t svc_thread_main_init(void) {
     g_main_handle = t->handle;
 #endif
     pthread_setspecific(g_keythr, t);
+    /* The game's main thread is the one that submits the frame (the NVN translation, 5 to 16 ms a frame outdoors). Unlike the
+       threads CreateThread makes (thread_main), it kept the launcher's QoS, unspecified: on a fanless MacBook Air M5 macOS moved it
+       to the efficiency cores a few minutes into play (the submit thread's clock 3.5 → 1.3-1.8 GHz, its CPU time 5 → 15 ms a frame,
+       Tears of the Kingdom outdoors at 40-50 fps with the GPU at 13 ms). User-interactive keeps it on the performance cores. */
+    pthread_set_qos_class_self_np(QOS_CLASS_USER_INTERACTIVE, 0);
     qos_class_t qc = QOS_CLASS_UNSPECIFIED; int rp = 0;
     pthread_get_qos_class_np(pthread_self(), &qc, &rp); t->qos = (uint32_t)qc;
     return t->handle;
